-- Dire Maul (map 429), Gordok Commons (north wing), 2026-11-13.
--
-- 1. Gordok Mastiff 13036 (53 spawns): unit_flags 33544 = 0x8308 has IMMUNE_TO_PC 0x100 and
--    PLAYER_CONTROLLED 0x8, so the hounds could not be attacked and never joined their ogres.
--    Pandaria 5.4.8 has 33280 (0x8200), AzerothCore 0. Removed 0x108: 33544 -> 33280.
-- 2. Guard Slip'kik 14323: unit_flags 295504 includes UNIT_FLAG_STUNNED 0x40000 (a sniff taken while
--    he was frozen in the Fixed Trap), so he never fought back. AzerothCore has 0. Removed 0x40000:
--    295504 -> 33360.
-- 3. Gordok Spirit 11446 (13 ghosts on the ledges around King Gordok's arena, emote only): unit_flags 512
--    left them hostile and attackable, so they pull into the King Gordok fight. Pandaria 5.4.8 has
--    768 (immune to players and NPCs), AzerothCore has them pacified. Added 0x100: 512 -> 768.
-- 4. Warpwood Pods (whole map): 262 pods stand on 67 spots, four on each (one of each variant
--    179526/179528/179532/179533). AzerothCore pools one pod per spot. Kept one lootable pod 179528
--    (lock 57, loot 16548) per spot; the three empty variants (no lock, no loot) are removed.
--    None of the removed pods has pool, event or SmartAI rows.
-- 5. Movement: Pandaria 5.4.8 paths for the same guids (5 patrols, paths 429002001+), AzerothCore
--    wander radius (50 Carrion Swarmers). Bosses, Mizzle, Knot, Cho'Rush and the Gordok Spirits are left alone.

-- 1. Gordok Mastiff
UPDATE `creature_template` SET `unit_flags` = `unit_flags` & ~264 WHERE `entry` = 13036;    -- 0x100 | 0x8

-- 2. Guard Slip'kik
UPDATE `creature_template` SET `unit_flags` = `unit_flags` & ~262144 WHERE `entry` = 14323; -- 0x40000

-- 3. Gordok Spirit
UPDATE `creature_template` SET `unit_flags` = `unit_flags` | 256 WHERE `entry` = 11446;   -- 0x100

-- 4. Warpwood Pods
